More often, it's smaller things, right?

27
00:00:59.850 --> 00:01:01.690
I mean, it's the things,

28
00:01:01.690 --> 00:01:04.290
in "Oprah", and I've talked about this a lot,

29
00:01:04.290 --> 00:01:05.460
we talked about this in the book.

30
00:01:05.460 --> 00:01:07.560
But one of the most important things

31
00:01:07.560 --> 00:01:11.210
about being a human being is feeling like you belong.

32
00:01:11.210 --> 00:01:12.720
Like you belong in your family,

33
00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:13.900
you belong in your community,

34
00:01:13.900 --> 00:01:15.990
you you belong in your culture.

35
00:01:15.990 --> 00:01:19.160
And if you get signals from your parents

36
00:01:19.160 --> 00:01:21.540
or you get signals from your classmates

37
00:01:21.540 --> 00:01:22.830
that you don't belong,

38
00:01:22.830 --> 00:01:24.860
and those signals might come from something

39
00:01:24.860 --> 00:01:29.120
