69
00:02:48.950 --> 00:02:50.250
I mean, if somebody tells me a teacher,

70
00:02:50.250 --> 00:02:52.820
I literally started like, "Oh, you're a teacher."

71
00:02:52.820 --> 00:02:57.710
Because in my life, teachers were my saviors.

72
00:02:57.710 --> 00:03:01.220
When I went to school, I was important.

73
00:03:01.220 --> 00:03:06.220
And that is where my sense of self and worthiness came from.

74
00:03:06.880 --> 00:03:10.230
Not from my family, but from other people.

75
00:03:10.230 --> 00:03:12.990
And so Bruce said, and this is true of all of us.

76
00:03:12.990 --> 00:03:15.240
Nobody makes it out here alone.

77
00:03:15.240 --> 00:03:18.650
And our connectedness to other people,

78
00:03:18.650 --> 00:03:21.460
our relationships with people who can see us,

79
00:03:21.460 --> 00:03:26.270
all you need is one person who fully sees you and believes.

80
00:03:26.270 --> 00:03:28.430
And that's the thing that you hold on to.

81
00:03:28.430 --> 00:03:32.530
That you are seen, you are valued, and that you matter.

82
